!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
Files
description: a whole text file of a given language
- >
  The node *is* a file: `file/json` (`.json`), `file/json5` (`.json5`), `file/json5p` (`.json5p`),
  `file/yaml` (`.yaml` / `.yml`), `file/yamlover` (`.yo`, plus the legacy `.yamlover` spelling — read
  forever, never written). Interior nodes take the same language without the `file/` prefix — the
  inlined forms.
- >
  A non-data **text material** — markdown, asciidoc, csv, plantuml — is modeled as a `file/yaml`
  scalar: its single value is the raw text, kept verbatim and rendered by its `format`. The format
  carries the real material type (`text/markdown`); the concrete only records "a text file holding one
  scalar" ([strings in their own file](::language:concretes:strings:own-file)).
